The Code Mode tool catalog has changed. This catalog supersedes the previous Code Mode tool catalog.

# Code Mode

The tools listed below, and `search`, cannot be called directly: they only work as JavaScript inside the `execute` tool. Every other tool you have is a normal tool call: call it directly, never inside `execute`.

The catalog is partial. Before calling a tool that is not listed below, find it with the global `search(...)` function. Do not guess tool names. Each result's `path` is the complete call expression: write it out as code, for example `await tools.ns.tool_name({ ... })`. Do not use it as a key such as `tools[path]`.

- search({
  query?: string,
  namespace?: string,
  /** @integer @exclusiveMinimum 0 */
  limit?: number,
  /** @integer @minimum 0 */
  offset?: number,
}): {
  items: Array<{
      path: string,
      description: string,
      signature: string,
    }>,
  /** @integer @minimum 0 */
  remaining: number,
  next: {
      /** @integer @minimum 0 */
      offset: number,
    } | null,
}

## Code Mode tools (call only inside `execute`)

- astgrep_debug_pattern (1 tool)
  - tools.astgrep_debug_pattern({
  /** Representative ast-grep pattern/snippet to parse, e.g. 'class A { $FIELD = $INIT }'. */
  pattern: string,
  /** Tree-sitter language to parse as. Always pass this. */
  lang: "bash" | "c" | "cpp" | "csharp" | "css" | "elixir" | "go" | "haskell" | "hcl" | "html" | "java" | "javascript" | "js" | "jsx" | "json" | "kotlin" | "lua" | "nix" | "php" | "python" | "ruby" | "rust" | "scala" | "solidity" | "swift" | "typescript" | "tsx" | "yaml",
  /** Debug output format. Defaults to cst; use cst for exact node kinds and ast for named nodes. */
  format?: "pattern" | "ast" | "cst" | "sexp" | null,
  /** Optional node kind to select from the parsed pattern. */
  selector?: string | null,
}): Promise<string | null> // Debug how ast-grep parses a query pattern without searching the codebase. Use cst to discover exact tree-sitter kinds...
- astgrep_pattern (1 tool)
  - tools.astgrep_pattern({
  /**
   * ast-grep pattern, e.g. 'app.get($ROUTE, $$$)' or 'class $NAME'. $VAR captures one node and $$$ captures zero or more nodes.
   */
  pattern: string,
  /** Tree-sitter language to parse as. Always pass this. */
  lang: "bash" | "c" | "cpp" | "csharp" | "css" | "elixir" | "go" | "haskell" | "hcl" | "html" | "java" | "javascript" | "js" | "jsx" | "json" | "kotlin" | "lua" | "nix" | "php" | "python" | "ruby" | "rust" | "scala" | "solidity" | "swift" | "typescript" | "tsx" | "yaml",
  /** File or directory to search. Defaults to the current session directory. */
  path?: string | null,
}): Promise<string | null> // Structural code search using ast-grep's simple pattern mode.
- astgrep_replace (1 tool)
  - tools.astgrep_replace({
  /** ast-grep pattern to search for, e.g. 'console.log($$$ARGS)'. */
  pattern: string,
  /** Replacement using metavariables captured by the pattern, e.g. 'logger.debug($$$ARGS)'. */
  rewrite: string,
  /** Tree-sitter language to parse as. Always pass this. */
  lang: "bash" | "c" | "cpp" | "csharp" | "css" | "elixir" | "go" | "haskell" | "hcl" | "html" | "java" | "javascript" | "js" | "jsx" | "json" | "kotlin" | "lua" | "nix" | "php" | "python" | "ruby" | "rust" | "scala" | "solidity" | "swift" | "typescript" | "tsx" | "yaml",
  /** File or directory to search. Defaults to the current session directory. */
  path?: string | null,
  /** When true, pass --update-all and modify files in place. Defaults to false for preview/dry-run. */
  apply?: boolean | null,
}): Promise<string | null> // Structural AST-aware search and replace using ast-grep's pattern/rewrite mode.
- astgrep_rule (1 tool)
  - tools.astgrep_rule({
  /**
   * YAML rule body (everything under rule:). This tool wraps it in {id, language, rule: <your yaml>}.
   *
   * Translate relational requests with has, inside, not, all, or any. ALWAYS add stopBy: end on every relational rule (inside/has/precedes/follows); otherwise ast-grep may stop at the first non-matching child.
   *
   * Use astgrep_debug_pattern with format cst to find node kind names. If a direct pattern is incomplete or ambiguous, use a pattern object with context and selector. Do not include a leading rule: key.
   */
  rule: string,
  /** Tree-sitter language to parse as. Always pass this. */
  lang: "bash" | "c" | "cpp" | "csharp" | "css" | "elixir" | "go" | "haskell" | "hcl" | "html" | "java" | "javascript" | "js" | "jsx" | "json" | "kotlin" | "lua" | "nix" | "php" | "python" | "ruby" | "rust" | "scala" | "solidity" | "swift" | "typescript" | "tsx" | "yaml",
  /** File or directory to search. Defaults to the current session directory. */
  path?: string | null,
}): Promise<string | null> // Structural code search using ast-grep YAML rule mode for relational or composite queries. Use inside, has, not, all, ...
- astgrep_test_pattern (1 tool)
  - tools.astgrep_test_pattern({
  /** ast-grep pattern to test. */
  pattern: string,
  /** Tree-sitter language to parse as. Always pass this. */
  lang: "bash" | "c" | "cpp" | "csharp" | "css" | "elixir" | "go" | "haskell" | "hcl" | "html" | "java" | "javascript" | "js" | "jsx" | "json" | "kotlin" | "lua" | "nix" | "php" | "python" | "ruby" | "rust" | "scala" | "solidity" | "swift" | "typescript" | "tsx" | "yaml",
  /** Small positive example code snippet that should match the pattern. */
  code: string,
